{
  "info": {
    "name": "FoC User Service",
    "description": "Sign-up, login and the session lifecycle for the FoC User Service. Set baseUrl and signupEmail in an environment; the OTP arrives in Mailpit at http://localhost:8025. AI Assistance Disclosure: Tool: Claude Code (model: Claude Opus 5), date: 2026-09-26. Scope: generated the collection for the three sign-up routes. Author review: every request run against the compose stack.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001"
    },
    {
      "key": "signupEmail",
      "value": "alex@u.nus.edu"
    },
    {
      "key": "otp",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "JWKS",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/.well-known/jwks.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Register",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"displayName\": \"Alex Tan\",\n  \"email\": \"{{signupEmail}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"+65\",\n  \"mobileNumber\": \"91234567\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rdSafe\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "201 with the new userId and when the code expires. No users row exists yet. Read the code in Mailpit, then set the `otp` variable."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Resend OTP",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register/resend-otp",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{signupEmail}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "202. Replaces the code inside a sign-up that is still waiting, without extending its 15-minute window. 404 if nothing is pending; 429 after three requests in ten minutes."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Verify registration",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Keeps the tokens in variables rather than in the file: nothing here is committed.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refreshToken);",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register/verify",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{signupEmail}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "200 with the auth response. The code is single-use, so replaying it gives OTP_EXPIRED."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Login",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "// Keeps the tokens in variables rather than in the file: nothing here is committed.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refreshToken);",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{signupEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rdSafe\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "200 with the auth response. 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS for a wrong password AND for an address with no account - the two are deliberately identical. Five failures in a row give 423 ACCOUNT_LOCKED with retryAfterSeconds, for 15 minutes."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Refresh",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Rotation invalidates the old token, so the stored pair must be replaced or the next",
              "// refresh looks like reuse and revokes every session.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refreshToken);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "200 with a new pair. Single use: sending the same refreshToken twice is treated as theft and revokes every session that user has. An unknown, an expired and a reused token all answer with the same 401."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Logout",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "204, always - an unknown or already-revoked token still means you are logged out. Needs the access token: the caller's identity comes from it, so you can only end your own session. Ends this session only; other devices keep theirs."
      }
    }
  ]
}
